        "anchor_id": "what-is-noopept",
        "kicker": "The basics",
        "heading": "What is Noopept?",
        "definition": "<p>Noopept (N-phenylacetyl-L-prolylglycine ethyl ester) is a <strong>peptide-like nootropic</strong> with structural similarities to racetams, but active at much smaller doses. It is valued for its <strong>rapid onset, subtle clarity, and studied neuroprotective properties</strong>, making it a favorite among experienced nootropic users and stack builders.</p>",
        "show_basics": true,
        "scientific_body": "<p><strong>Compound:</strong> N-phenylacetyl-L-prolylglycine ethyl ester, a dipeptide. Noopept is reported to modulate <strong>glutamatergic (AMPA/NMDA)</strong> and <strong>acetylcholine</strong> pathways tied to learning and memory, and studies describe increased expression of <strong>BDNF and NGF</strong> in the hippocampus. Onset is typically 20–30 minutes; effects are subtle and build with consistent use.</p><ul><li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> glutamate/acetylcholine modulation; upregulation of BDNF and NGF in animal models.</li><li><strong>Rationale:</strong> potent at micro-doses (10–30 mg) versus gram-dose racetams.</li><li><strong>Forms:</strong> pre-measured 20 mg capsules, or powder for users who prefer to weigh their own servings.</li></ul><p><em>Human evidence remains limited. Informational only. Not medical advice.</em></p>",
        "scientific_collapsed": true,
        "molecule_alt": "Noopept molecule diagram",
        "molecule_decorative": true,
        "hide_image_mobile": false,
        "max_width": 1200,
        "padding_top": 96,
        "padding_bottom": 96,
        "center_on_mobile": false,
        "show_note": true,
        "note_text": "This content is educational and not medical advice. Noopept is for adult use only. Start at the lowest dose to assess tolerance. Consult a healthcare professional if you take medication."
      }
